        "original_id": "43756f89-4822-51aa-8a9c-4c6994f8611b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Morgan State University, University of Idaho\n- People: Lyttleton Morgan\n- Places: Maryland, Idaho, Moscow, Latah County\n- Topics: HBCUs, public universities, university naming\n\nFacts:\n- Morgan State University was founded as the Centenary Biblical Institute.\n- Reverend Lyttleton Morgan was the first chairman of the board of trustees of Morgan State University.\n- Morgan State University was later renamed in honor of Lyttleton Morgan.\n- The University of Idaho is Idaho's oldest public university.\n- The University of Idaho is located in Moscow in Latah County in northern Idaho.\n- The University of Idaho is officially abbreviated UI and is locally referred to as \"the U of I.\"\n- Morgan State University is Maryland's designated public urban university.\n- Morgan State University is the largest HBCU in Maryland.",
